<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Horror, (Some) Comedy, Sci-Fi</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Article Format</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Elevator Pitch:</p>
<p>⦁ A seemingly unassuming small hotel in the Mojave Desert</p>
<p>⦁ The interior is infinitely larger than the exterior</p>
<p>⦁ The motel is a fixed point in multiple realities</p>
<p>⦁ There's no observable staff from outside, but inside there is</p>
<p>⦁ Those who have seen the staff cannot recall any physical features, only that they are polite and courteous</p>
<p>⦁ Some staff have personalities that can be recalled, but that is the only memorable trait they have</p>
<p>⦁ Those who stay past check out are escorted out by security, also whose features are unable to be recalled</p>
<p>⦁ Occasionally, those that check in are altered to have an anomalous ability/property, and it is hinted by the staff that that's one of the reasons why they are drawn in</p>
<p>⦁ The halls are infinite and labyrinthine</p>
<p>⦁ The motel rooms are generic and normal-seeming</p>
<p>⦁ The motel room windows each look out on different worlds</p>
<p>⦁ Some people who leave the motel are from alternate Earths</p>
<p>⦁ Despite the monitoring and security, somehow, sometimes some people manage to get past to check in</p>
<p>⦁ An exploration log will be included, detailing science teams with armed escorts as well as D-class personnel teams exploring the Motel's interior</p>
<p>⦁ A breach log which will detail instances where civilians attempt to gain entry to the site, have gained entry, as well as those who managed to make it into the motel. This log will also include instances where those who entered are recovered. It will also detail instances where on-site personnel themselves attempted to check in to the motel.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: World-building</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: The motel occasionally has a guest who stays in a room that looks out onto our world, and the dressers are filled with money from different time periods and countries, some of which no longer exist or have never existed. And the money includes ancient drachmas, crudely carved red painted stones, and etc.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Additional Notes: I'm not sure where I need help, but I gladly accept any advice willing to be given!</p>

