<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Gryphon Watcher. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>So your Elevator Pitch has gotten me intrigued. It sorta reminds me of the Interdimensional Diner in <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4258">SCP-4258</a>. There are loads of opportunities to take such a concept and I’m also glad to see you playing around with some of those ideas with manipulating the physical space and thinking about its inhabitants.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Central Narrative: World-building</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don’t understand what you mean by this, though. If you mean ‘world-building’ as description of the setting, I’m afraid that’s not the same thing as having an actual storyline for us to follow. Are you planning on having an exploration log? How will you be showing us around the hotel? Even SCP-4258 had distinct characters that followed through each time the Foundation visited – who do we meet at your hotel besides an assortment of guests?</p>
<p>That’s my main issue at the moment: it’s not enough to simply have a cool setting. What are you going to do with it, who are the main characters involved and why are the stakes high enough for the Foundation to get involved? I hope you can elaborate on these pointers.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise your concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll do my best to reply. All the best for now!</p>

