				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gryphon-watcher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7004233); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7004233&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607482244" alt="Gryphon Watcher" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7004233)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gryphon-watcher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7004233); return false;" >Gryphon Watcher</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607246653 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 09:24</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837792">
									

<p>The exploration logs involve singular as well as small groups of D-Class personnel, as well as scientists with armed escorts. They will do things like talk to the staff and try to get pictures of them (which are always blurry on the faces of said staff) and try to map out the endless halls, which seems to shift suddenly, but not in any perceptible way. Also, I figure that they would also try sending in a drone like with the Endless Ikea. The exploration logs will all involve those who enter having a very hard time finding their way back to the front desk and exit. Sometimes they find it on their own, other times the staff or security helps them, and sometimes they are never heard from again. They even sometimes return with individuals who have been lost for years. Some of then come from alternate Earths. There are even others who, while not appearing human, insist that they are human, and that their strange appearances is normal on the Earth they are from. Also, some of those who leave have anomalous properties/abilities, having been altered by the motel through an event that they cannot recall the details of. The log will also include encounters with the entities from the various worlds viewed from the rooms through the windows.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>And for the breach log, that will be similar to the exploration log, in that those who check in will sometimes find their way back out on their own, be escorted by the staff, or disappear, sometimes forever. Of course, there will be the accounts of on-site personnel trying to apprehend them. Some will be from them trying to drive onto the site, being turned away in a daze. Others will insist that they have an appointment at the motel, even becoming belligerent and/or violent. (One such example of that being the entire biker gang that drove up claiming to have an appointment.) This will be a daily occurrence of at least two or three instances. But then there are others that, as though the fence surrounding it weren't there, drove into the parking lot, always when no one was observing. Those are always surprised to be caught, if the on-site personnel can get to them in time, completely oblivious to being in a restricted area. That's a bit rarer. Once every couple of months or so. And then, there's said on-site personnel who, for reasons that they themselves cannot remember, also try to check in.</p>
<p>As for it's nature… well, it's (theorized) a fixed point in many different alternate universes that exists as is, despite being in locations where it makes no sense for a motel like itself to exist in. (I.e. the bottom of an ocean, near an altar, in a swamp, etc.) It's origins are unknown, and if the staff know they are refusing to answer, but it's goal seems to be to draw in &quot;guests&quot;, in some cases with an intent to give them anomalous properties/abilities. Said abilities are seemingly random.</p>
</div>
</div>
