														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839350">
									

<p>Hi Gryphon Watcher, thank you for your elaboration.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It's origins are unknown, and if the staff know they are refusing to answer, but it's goal seems to be to draw in &quot;guests&quot;, in some cases with an intent to give them anomalous properties/abilities.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hmm. This is still the part that's problematic for me. You've described A LOT of various anomalous properties that the hotel manifests, and I get that it's a place of intersecting universes, so this kind of randomness is to be expected.</p>
<p>But you need to have an explanation for the base anomaly. What exactly are its origins, and why does it want to draw guests in and turn them into anomalies themselves. I feel that if you were to explore this strand further, <strong>this</strong> will be your Central Narrative and the basis of your breaching and exploration logs. The Foundation has to investigate the anomaly and ultimately reach a conclusion of sorts. What is this conclusion?</p>
<p>Right now, the description sounds very cool, but it also sounds like an episode of Interdimensional Cable from <em>Rick &amp; Morty</em> (you should check it out). While it's cool for a while to see random things happening, there has to be an underlying narrative that ties things together. Otherwise, it's just a series of random occurences and there's no payoff.</p>
<p>For what it's worth, I think you're on the right track, and you're close to a greenlight from me. Continue expanding on what the end goal of the article will look like?</p>

							</div>

								
					
